ransition-colors\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L1a\\\",null,{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"iconNode\\\":[[\\\"path\\\",{\\\"d\\\":\\\"m15 18-6-6 6-6\\\",\\\"key\\\":\\\"1wnfg3\\\"}]],\\\"className\\\":\\\"lucide-chevron-left h-4 w-4\\\",\\\"aria-hidden\\\":true}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"max-w-[10rem] truncate sm:max-w-xs\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Shri Vanchhara Parshwanath\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{}]]}]\\n1f:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"footer\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-auto border-t border-sandstone-deep/60 py-8\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 font-ui text-xs text-ink-soft flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-2 sm:items-center sm:justify-between\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"१०८ पार्श्वनाथ तीर्थ दर्शन — श्री पार्श्वनाथ भगवान के तीर्थों का डिजिटल संकलन\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Original source: Rajendra Kumar Jain, Parshv Sadan, Parshv Nagar, Dungarpur\\\"}]]}]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"24:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"6\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Directions: Khambhat is a very popular port city of Gujarat, well connected by rail and road to other cities. This temple is 1.5 km from the railway station. Dharamshala and bhojanshala facilities, as well as jnanabhandars holding many ancient books and scriptures, are available here.\\\"}]\\n25:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"7\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Hymn of Praise: Beholding your wondrous image, my eyes find peace; I have come to you to claim the kingdom of liberation; I have accepted you as my mother and father — fulfil my heartfelt wish and carry me across. \\\\\\\"With loving devotion I bow in reverence to Shri Ratna Chintamani Lord Parshwa.\\\\\\\"\\\"}]\\n26:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"8\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Chanting Mantra: \\\\\\\"Om Hreem Arham, Shri Ratna Chintamani Parshwanathaya Namah\\\\\\\"\\\"}]\\n27:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"9\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Shrine Address: Shri Ratna Chintamani Parshwanath Shwetambar Jain Tirth, Manek Chowk, Mu.Po. Khambhat, Dist. Kheda, via Anand (Gujarat) 388620. Phone Number – 02698226006. Contacts: 1. Shri Tejasbhai – Khambhat 9898536939, 2. Shri Girishbhai – Mumbai 09320362702.\\\"}]\\n2d:T4cb,The Life of the Reverend (Purushdaniya) Arhat Parshwanath, Part 18 (Nirvana and the Site): After his life as a householder, taking diksha, and remaining for 83 days and nights in the state prior to omniscience (chhadmastha), he attained omniscience (kevalgyan) and, living as an omniscient ascetic (kevali) for 70 years, observing the life of a shraman, the Reverend Arhat Parshwanath lived out his full lifespan of one hundred years. When his karmas of feeling (vedaniya), lifespan (dirghayu), name (nama), and lineage (gotra) were exhausted, in the fourth ara (dushama-sushama) of the descending half-cycle of time (avasarpini kal), in the first month of the rainy season, in its second fortnight — that is, on the eighth day of the bright half of the month of Shravan — on Mount Sammet Shikhar, together with thirty-four persons (Parshwanath himself and 33 other monks), after a month-long fast upon the mountain, observing a waterless fast (chovihar), as morning came and the conjunction of the Vishakha constellation arrived, he remained fixed in the posture of kayotsarga meditation and, attaining the state beyond karma (kaldharma), achieved liberation (moksha) — thus becoming free from all suffering. ...The End.28:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"10\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"$2d\\\"}]\\n29:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"11\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Compiled by: Rajendra Kumar Jain, Parshwa Sadan, Parshwa Nagar, Dungarpur, Rajasthan. Rkjainasp – 8107105235.\\\"}]\\n2a:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"12\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Please forward this PDF book on WhatsApp and save it on your mobile device, so that whenever you travel to that region for pilgrimage, you can open Google Maps to find information about the nearby shrine of Lord Parshwanath and travel with ease.\\\"}]\\n2b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"13\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"If, in the compilation of this book, anything has been written against scripture or dharma — whether through a stray mark, diacritic, or otherwise — I seek forgiveness in thought, word, and deed (Michhami Dukkadam).\\\"}]\\n2c:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"14\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Jai Jinendra from Rajendra Kumar Jain and family.\\\"}]\\n\"])</script></body></html>","rscData":"","segmentData":{"/_tree":"","/_full":"","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug/__PAGE__":"","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug":"","/$d$lang/tirtha":"","/$d$lang":"","/_index":"","/_head":""},"headers":{"x-nextjs-stale-time":"300","x-nextjs-prerender":"1","x-next-cache-tags":"_N_T_/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/tirtha/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/tirtha/[slug]/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/tirtha/[slug]/page,_N_T_/en/tirtha/tirtha-139"},"segmentPaths":["/_tree","/_full","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug/__PAGE__","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug","/$d$lang/tirtha","/$d$lang","/_index","/_head"],"revalidate":60,"cacheControl":{"revalidate":60,"expire":31536000}}}